DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261123
SUMMARY:[Curated Role Feeds] US Department of Labor proposes to update fid
 uciary rule to affirm Employee Retirement Income Security Act’s exclusiv
 e purpose rule
DESCRIPTION:WASHINGTON – The U.S. Department of Labor’s Employee Benef
 its Security Administration today issued proposed amendments to the invest
 ment duties regulation to clarify the fiduciary duty of loyalty under the 
 Employee Retirement Income Security Act.The proposed rule seeks to end the
  32-year uncertainty surrounding whether ERISA allows fiduciaries to consi
 der non-financial factors in retirement plan investments\, including envir
 onmental\, social\, and governance\, and diversity\, equity\, and inclusio
 n. The proposal gives fiduciaries an affirmative expression of their duty 
 of loyalty\, which would clarify that ERISA requires plan fiduciaries to a
 ct solely in the interest of the plan’s participants and beneficiaries\,
  and for the exclusive purpose of providing for the interests of participa
 nts and beneficiaries in their retirement income or financial benefits und
 er the plan.“President Trump’s Department of Labor is not putting its 
 thumb on the scale for or against any particular investment or asset class
 \,” said U.S. Secretary of Labor Keith Sonderling. “Our proposed rule 
 makes clear that retirement plan fiduciaries must make investment decision
 s solely in the financial interests of workers and retirees\, not to advan
 ce political or social agendas. Our focus is on protecting and growing Ame
 ricans’ retirement savings\, which have reached record levels thanks to 
 President Trump.”If finalized\, the proposal would also place a heighten
 ed focus on shareholder engagement and proxy voting by fiduciaries to secu
 re the retirement interests of American workers and would avoid the improp
 er pressures and influence placed on plan fiduciaries. This includes votin
 g shares and otherwise attempting to influence corporate behavior through 
 shareholder engagement activities for ESG/DEI purposes. The proposed rule 
 follows the directive in President Trump’s executive order\, “Protecti
 ng American Investors from Foreign-Owned and Politically Motivated Proxy A
 dvisors\,” which instructed the department to stre\nhttp://www.dol.gov/n
 ewsroom/releases/ebsa/ebsa20261123
URL:http://www.dol.gov/newsroom/releases/ebsa/ebsa20261123
CATEGORIES:Curated Role Feeds
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
